# The leftovers: the names of what the team's test runs and scripts leave in /tmp and /var/tmp,
# which team-janitor tmp (bin/lib/tmp.sh) removes once stale. It reads this file from its own
# checkout, so the names it may remove change only through a reviewed PR.
# One line per name: the maker (a project's registry name, or bats), one space, then an extended
# regular expression matched against the whole name of an entry, case-sensitively. A # line and a
# blank line are comments.
# A line may only be a name that the team's test runs alone make, or its scripts alone: a run's
# list of its temporary paths (bin/lib/temp-files.sh's team-temp.<pid>.<random>), which a KILL
# leaves and team-janitor tmp removes alone, as a regular file whose pid is no live process of
# this user's, never the paths it names. Its expression begins with a literal of at least 6
# characters, holds no | (an alternation would match past that literal), and never matches
# mktemp's default (tmp.XXXXXXXXXX), which any program makes, nor what systemd, Claude Code,
# Chrome, Node or pytest keep there. tests/repo.bats holds each line to that, and team-janitor tmp
# refuses to run with a line holding a |.
no-mistakes nm-cli-home-[0-9]+
no-mistakes nm-cli-test-[0-9]+
no-mistakes nm-timeout-bin-[0-9]+
no-mistakes nm-update-test-[0-9]+
no-mistakes nm-update-home-[0-9]+
no-mistakes git-template-[0-9]+
no-mistakes fakecli-helper-[0-9]+
bats bats-run-[A-Za-z0-9]{6}
agent-team team-checks\.[A-Za-z0-9]{6}
agent-team compaction-drill\.[A-Za-z0-9]{6}
agent-team team-temp\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+
conventioner real-mongo-test\.[A-Za-z0-9]{6,10}
conventioner nmtest-[0-9]+-venv\.[A-Za-z0-9]{6,10}
